{{Quote|The name's Remy LeBeau. Le diable blanc.<ref name="Devil">Translates from Cajun/Creole French to "''The White Devil.''"</ref> But you can call me the Gambit.|Gambit to [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
'''Remy Etienne LeBeau''' is a [[Mutants|mutant]] with the ability to manipulate kinetic energy, displaying a talent for card throwing and using a [[Gambit's Bō Staff|bō staff]]. Having eventually taken the name '''Gambit''', he was banished to the [[Void]] by the [[Time Variance Authority]], where he joined a resistance group to battle [[Cassandra Nova]] and her forces. He and his team forged an alliance with [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] to defeat Cassandra and escape the Void.

==Biography==
===Life in the Void===
{{Quote|Maybe I was born [[Void|here]], it's hard to know for sure.|Gambit|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Remy LeBeau resided in the [[Void]] as a kinetic energy manipulative mutant dubbed Gambit, with no knowledge of his prior life. While in the Void, he met [[Elektra/Forgotten Elektra|Elektra]], [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]], [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Human Torch]], [[Quicksilver/Anchor Being Wolverine|Quicksilver]], [[Punisher/Resistant Punisher|Punisher]] and [[Daredevil/Forgotten Elektra|Daredevil]], who were members of the [[Resistance]], a group that opposed the rule of oppresive omega-level mutant [[Cassandra Nova]]. Gambit fought alongside the Resistance members, and witnessed the deaths of Quicksilver, Punisher and Daredevil.{{Ref|DW}}

===Meeting Deadpool===
{{Quote|They call me the Gambit."<br>"Do they? You sure you didn't just really, really want them to, but it {{WPS|Gambit (unproduced film)|never quite worked out}}?|Gambit and [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
{{Rewrite}}
Gambit and the other resistance members met [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]], who did the impossible and escaped Nova's lair alive. They also learned that [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Human Torch]] was killed by Cassandra, but Deadpool left out the reason why he died. Eventually, Deadpool convinced him and the others to invade [[Cassandra Nova's Compound]] to avenge Storm's death and take her down using [[Juggernaut]]'s [[Juggernaut's Helmet|helmet]] to block her powers. However, Wolverine scoffed that their plan was doomed to fail and refused to join them.{{Ref|DW}}

===[[Attack on Cassandra Nova's Compound|Getting an Ending]]===
{{Quote|You know how long I been waiting for this? Whoo, I'm aboutta make a name for myself here.|Gambit|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Gambit traveled in the [[Nicepool]]'s {{WPS|Honda Odyssey (North America)|Honda Odyssey}}, [[Ol' Betsy]] with the Resistance to finally invade Cassandra's fortress. [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]] used [[Punisher/Resistant Punisher|Punisher]]'s {{WPS|AT4|AT4 Rocket Launcher}} to break into their base and them held off [[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|Nova's forces]], as Deadpool and Wolverine went off to confront her while [[X-23|X-23]] secured the helmet. Later in the battle as [[Alioth]] approached the compound, Gambit witnessed [[Deadpool]] and [[Wolverine]] jump into a [[Inter-Dimensional Portal]] created by Cassandra who gave the duo a way home after they saved her life from [[Pyro]]. He was later returned to his home reality by the [[Time Variance Authority]] at Deadpool's request.{{Ref|DW}}

