==Trivia==
*In the comics, Gambit is depicted as a former thief and long-standing member of the [[X-Men]]. He is also a love interest to Rogue.
*Gambit is one character who was portrayed by an actor that exists in the Marvel Cinematic Universe without portraying themselves, alongside [[Mainframe]] and [[Blade/Universe Defender Blade|Blade]]. [[Channing Tatum]]'s existence in the MCU was confirmed in the ''[[Jessica Jones (TV series)|Jessica Jones]]'' episode ''[[AKA Ladies Night]]''.

==Behind the Scenes==
*Gambit in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] fulfills [[Channing Tatum]]'s long desire to portray Gambit on screen in a film rather than continue the previous on-screen version. Tatum was originally supposed to portray Gambit in a {{WPS|Gambit (unproduced film)|long in-development film}} that was subsequently cancelled following the {{WPS|Acquisition of 21st Century Fox by Disney|acquisition of 20th Century Fox by Disney}}.
*Gambit in the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]] is the second live-action incarnation of the character, following an incarnation portrayed by {{WPS|Taylor Kitsch}}.
*[[David MacDonald]] was a stunt double for [[Channing Tatum]] in the role of Gambit.

